                    "q": "(Simple and Compound Sentences): What is a simple sentence and what is a compound sentence? Give examples and the linking words.",
                    "a": "A simple sentence usually has a single verb. It has a subject, a verb, and a completed thought. Example: Jamil plays tennis every Saturday. (Jamil = subject, plays = verb). A compound sentence is made up of two independent clauses (or complete sentences) connected to one another with a linking word. Example: Jamil plays tennis every Saturday but this Saturday he is playing golf. Linking words are easy to remember if you think of the word FANBOYS: For, And, Nor, But, Or, Yet, So. There are other linking words also, e.g., because, as, etc."
