                    "q": ". Write the summary of the poem.",
                    "a": "The poem 'Speak Gently' by David Bates teaches us to speak gently to everyone. It is better to rule by love than by fear, and harsh words can spoil the good we do. We should speak gently to little children to win their love and teach them softly, because childhood does not last long. We should speak gently to old people and not grieve their tired hearts, because their sands of life are nearly run and they should depart in peace. Speaking gently is a small thing, but it drops into the heart's deep well and brings good and joy that will last forever. Eternity shall tell of its good results."
