                    "a": "The basis of soft drinks, the syrup, is made up of water, sugar, acid, coloring and flavoring agents. This syrup is prepared by dissolving these ingredients into water to 65 Brix. The material required for the preparation of a soft drink is: (1) Water (2) Calcium and other minerals (3) Coloring and flavoring agent (4) Sugar for microbial growth (5) Citric acid for sour taste.",
