                    "a": "(a) Electromagnetic waves are transverse waves produced by oscillating electric and magnetic fields; they are radiated out when charged particles oscillate, and they can travel through a vacuum. (b) In decreasing order of wavelength (longest to shortest): radio waves, microwaves, infrared radiation, visible light, ultraviolet radiation, X-rays, gamma rays. (c) No. All electromagnetic waves travel through space or a vacuum at the same speed, c = 3×10^8 m/s, whatever their frequency.",
