                    "a": "Industrial radiography is a technique of inspecting materials to detect inside defects by using high-frequency X-rays. A beam of x-rays points at the tested item and a detector is aligned with the beam on the other side of the item. The detector records the x-rays that pass through the material. The thicker the material, the fewer x-rays can pass through; more rays move through the region where the material is thinner (a crack or flaw), so the detector computes a picture from the rays that pass through, which shows cracks or flaws in that material.",
