                    "a": "(a) The near point is the closest point at which the eye can focus clearly (25 cm for a normal eye); the far point is the farthest point at which the eye can see clearly (infinity for a normal eye). (b) The ciliary muscles change the curvature of the eye lens: to focus on near objects the muscles contract and the lens becomes more convex (shorter focal length); to focus on distant objects the muscles relax and the lens becomes flatter (longer focal length).",
                    "q": "(a) What is the difference between the near point and the far point of the eye? (b) How does the eye lens change its shape to focus on objects at different distances?"
