                    "a": "The field of data storage has improved a lot: images recorded in digital cameras can be transferred to computers where they can be edited easily. The record of a person such as an ID card, passport, driving license, insurance card, health card and biometric data (voice scan or eye-retina scan) can all be stored on a single tiny chip. The telephone signals which were transmitted electrically through copper wires are now transmitted digitally (as light) through optical fibers. Equipment used in the film industry for recording (camera, sound recorder, audio visual recording tape) has been replaced by digital cameras, which perform all these operations with better resolution and accuracy.",
