                    "a": "Genetic engineering is the artificial manipulation, modification and recombination of DNA or other nucleic acid molecules in order to modify an organism or population of organisms; it refers to any process in which an organism's genome is intentionally altered. It does not encompass traditional breeding techniques, because it requires manipulation of an organism's genes through cloning or transformation via the addition of foreign DNA.",
