                    "a": "(a) The main scale reading is 3.9 cm and the 9th line of the Vernier scale coincides with the main scale, so the Vernier reading is 9 × 0.01 = 0.09 cm. Total reading = 3.9 + 0.09 = 3.99 cm. (b) The Screw Gauge gives the most precise measurement, because its least count is 0.01 mm, while the least count of the Vernier caliper is 0.01 cm and that of the meter rule is 1 mm."
