                    "a": "The moment of force is the turning effect of a force, that is, the tendency to rotate a body about an axis. It is also called torque. Torque depends on the magnitude of the force and the perpendicular distance from the axis to the point of application of the force; torque = force × perpendicular distance. [[S]](i) Find the force: torque = force × length[[/S]][[E]]300 = force × 0.3[[/E]][[E]]force = 300/0.3 = 1000 N[[/E]][[S]](ii) Find the length for a torque of 500 Nm with the same force: 500 = 1000 × length[[/S]][[E]]length = 500/1000 = 0.5 m[[/E]][[A]](i) The force applied is 1000 N, (ii) the length of the spanner should be 0.5 m.[[/A]]"
