              {
                "label": "Efficiency",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "q": "Calculate the efficiency of a machine which consumes 200 J of energy and performs 50J of work.",
                    "a": "[[S]]Write down the given quantities:[[/S]][[E]]Input = 200 J[[/E]][[E]]Output = 50 J[[/E]][[S]]Write the formula:[[/S]][[E]]Efficiency = (Output / Input) × 100[[/E]][[S]]Put the values:[[/S]][[E]]Efficiency = (50 / 200) × 100[[/E]][[S]]Calculate:[[/S]][[E]]Efficiency = 25%[[/E]][[A]]The efficiency of the machine is 25%.[[/A]]"
                  },
                  {
                    "q": "Write a note on efficiency.",
                    "a": "The ratio of the energy given to a system (input) and the energy obtained from it (output) is called efficiency. Efficiency = (output energy / input energy) × 100. It has no unit. No machine is 100% efficient, because some energy is always wasted in the form of heat, sound or light."
                  },
                  {
                    "q": "If the efficiency of a machine is 70% and its output is 100 J then calculate its input.",
                    "a": "[[S]]Write down the given quantities:[[/S]][[E]]Efficiency = 70% = 0.70[[/E]][[E]]Output = 100 J[[/E]][[S]]Write the formula:[[/S]][[E]]Efficiency = Output / Input[[/E]][[S]]Arrange the formula for Input:[[/S]][[E]]Input = Output / Efficiency[[/E]][[S]]Put the values:[[/S]][[E]]Input = 100 / 0.70[[/E]][[S]]Calculate:[[/S]][[E]]Input = 142.86 J[[/E]][[A]]The input of the machine is 142.86 J.[[/A]]"
                  },
                  {
                    "q": "Which machine is more efficient, machine \"A\" which has an output of 200J after consuming 400J of energy or machine \"B\" which has an output of 300J after consuming 450J of energy?",
                    "a": "[[S]]Find the efficiency of machine A:[[/S]][[E]]Efficiency = (200 / 400) × 100 = 50%[[/E]][[S]]Find the efficiency of machine B:[[/S]][[E]]Efficiency = (300 / 450) × 100 = 66.67%[[/E]][[A]]Machine B is more efficient, because its efficiency is 66.67%, which is greater than machine A's 50%.[[/A]]"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "Power",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "q": "Define power.",
                    "a": "The rate of doing work is called power; that is, the work done or the energy transferred per unit time."
                  },
                  {
                    "q": "The energy of 600J dissipated by a bulb in 50 minutes. Find the power of the bulb.",
                    "a": "[[S]]Write down the given quantities:[[/S]][[E]]W = 600 J[[/E]][[E]]t = 50 minutes = 50 × 60 = 3000 s[[/E]][[S]]Write the formula:[[/S]][[E]]P = W / t[[/E]][[S]]Put the values:[[/S]][[E]]P = 600 / 3000[[/E]][[S]]Calculate:[[/S]][[E]]P = 0.2 W[[/E]][[A]]The power of the bulb is 0.2 W.[[/A]]"
                  },
                  {
                    "q": "Convert 20watt into horse power.",
                    "a": "[[S]]Write down the given quantities:[[/S]][[E]]P = 20 W[[/E]][[E]]1 hp = 746 W[[/E]][[S]]Write the formula:[[/S]][[E]]Power (in hp) = Power (in W) / 746[[/E]][[S]]Put the values:[[/S]][[E]]Power = 20 / 746[[/E]][[S]]Calculate:[[/S]][[E]]Power = 0.0268 hp[[/E]][[A]]20 watt = 0.027 hp.[[/A]]"
                  },
                  {
                    "q": "Calculate the power of a machine, if it does 40 joules of work in 10 sec.",
                    "a": "[[S]]Write down the given quantities:[[/S]][[E]]W = 40 J[[/E]][[E]]t = 10 s[[/E]][[S]]Write the formula:[[/S]][[E]]P = W / t[[/E]][[S]]Put the values:[[/S]][[E]]P = 40 / 10[[/E]][[S]]Calculate:[[/S]][[E]]P = 4 W[[/E]][[A]]The power of the machine is 4 W.[[/A]]"
                  },
                  {
                    "q": "Define Watt.",
                    "a": "The power of a body is called one watt if it works at the rate of one joule per second."
                  },
                  {
                    "q": "A student of weight 400N takes 5 sec to climb up an obstacle of height 2m. Calculate the power consumed.",
                    "a": "[[S]]First find the work:[[/S]][[E]]W = F × d = 400 × 2 = 800 J[[/E]][[S]]Write down the given quantities:[[/S]][[E]]W = 800 J[[/E]][[E]]t = 5 s[[/E]][[S]]Write the formula:[[/S]][[E]]P = W / t[[/E]][[S]]Put the values:[[/S]][[E]]P = 800 / 5[[/E]][[S]]Calculate:[[/S]][[E]]P = 160 W[[/E]][[A]]The power consumed by the student is 160 W.[[/A]]"
                  },
                  {
                    "q": "Write down the names of any two larger units of power.",
                    "a": "Kilowatt (kW) and Megawatt (MW)."
                  },
                  {
                    "q": "If a machine consumes 250J of energy per hour then what will be its power?",
                    "a": "[[S]]Write down the given quantities:[[/S]][[E]]W = 250 J[[/E]][[E]]t = 1 hour = 3600 s[[/E]][[S]]Write the formula:[[/S]][[E]]P = W / t[[/E]][[S]]Put the values:[[/S]][[E]]P = 250 / 3600[[/E]][[S]]Calculate:[[/S]][[E]]P = 0.0694 W[[/E]][[A]]The power of the machine is 0.0694 W (about 0.07 W).[[/A]]"
                  }
                ]
              }
