                    "q": "Q2. A large aquarium for fish is filled with water. The weight of the aquarium with the water in it is 10000N. The base of the aquarium has an area of 1.6m^2. Calculate the pressure exerted on the base of the aquarium by the water.",
                    "a": "[[E]]Pressure = Force/Area = F/A[[/E]][[S]]Force = F = 10000 N[[/S]][[S]]Area = A = 1.6 m^2[[/S]][[S]]P = 10000/1.6[[/S]][[A]]P = 6250 Pa[[/A]]"
