                  {
                    "q": "What is space debris? How can it be reduced?",
                    "a": "Space debris is non-operational space junk that remains in space after it has been utilized — old satellites, rocket parts, and even small pieces like a paint fleck or a screw. It pollutes the nearby space around Earth, and collisions with operational satellites, astronauts or space stations may endanger future missions. It can be reduced by: minimizing the release of mission-related objects; safeguarding the physical integrity of astronauts, rocket bodies and spacecraft; and taking measures to reduce the chances of collisions of satellites/space debris."
                  }
