                    "a": "In a country citizens enjoy three types of rights: (1) Civil rights — protection of life, protection from physical torture and inhuman treatment, not being arrested or exiled, freedom of movement, freedom of thought and expression and freedom of religion. (2) Political rights — freedom of expression, freedom of association and assembly, the right to vote and take part in elections. (3) Economic and social rights — the right to work, the right to property, a fair wage, the right to education, health, food, housing and a proper standard of life.",
